      "text": "Since the novel was first published in 1856, and the original author (Flaubert) has been deceased long enough (over 70 years), the original text *and* older English translations are in the **public domain** in many parts of the world, meaning they are often legally available to read online for free.\n\nThe search results confirm that it is a widely available classic. To give you the most specific confirmation and potential links, I should try to find a source that explicitly lists the public domain translations.\n\nSince the general searches pointed back to Wikipedia and general book pages, I will try a more targeted search to see if I can find direct evidence of accessible translations. (Note: Both initial searches returned the same general results, which suggests the specific translation information is not on the first few organic result pages.)",
